※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 8501 IMPL_BACKEND_UNSUPPORTED

※ Division writes its quotient and its remainder to a fixed pair of registers
※ on one of the three targets, which the register allocator cannot yet be told
※ about.  Refused on every target rather than on the one that cannot do it, so
※ that a program means the same thing wherever it is compiled.

let twenty: u8 = 20u8
let four: u8 = 4u8

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    twenty ÷ four
